      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are highlighting a key argument that bureaucratic hurdles can impede the speed of iteration critical to startup success. Heavy regulation can indeed create significant compliance costs, acting as a more substantial barrier to entry for lean startups than for established, well-resourced corporations. However, some argue that this speed comes at the cost of ethical or societal risk, suggesting regulation is necessary to govern areas like data privacy as technologies mature.",
      "source": "target",
